Z||000009||Cheever3000||08-28-2001||10:39 AM||||Okay, um, was it <I>your</I> words that were spoken that turned the wheels and caused the tears?  If so, I would think some apology would be in order before you start talking about <I>needing</I> her(him?) to be there.  And once cords have been broken, you've pretty much been cut loose, I'm sorry to say.  Same with burnt bridges, only that usually implies that you only have yourself to blame.  The rest of it is kind of a wordy way of saying you should stay together even if things get bad, but with the right music it could be fine.  Lots of popular songs have lyrics that make NO sense whatsoever, so you've got an advantage, IMO.<BR>||||reg||1
